    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25381" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jūrĭdĭcĭālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>relating to right</i> or <i>justice</i>
			(class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juridicialis constitutio est, cum factum
					convenit, sed jure, an injuria factum sit, quaeritur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 1, 14, 24</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv. 2, 23, 69</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 22, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Top. 24, 92</span></i>
			.</div>
